D2E1:              
D2E1:              ; THIS ROUTINE IS USED TO ASCERTAIN THAT A GIVEN
D2E1:              ; NUMBER OF LOCS REMAIN AVAILABLE FOR THE STACK.
D2E1:              ;    THE CALL IS:
D2E1:              ;	LDA #NUMBER OF 2-BYTE ENTRIES NEEDED.
D2E1:              ;	JSR	GETSTK
D2E1:              
D2E1:              ; THIS ROUTINE MUST BE CALLED BY ANY ROUTINE WHICH PUTS
D2E1:              ; AN ARBITRARY AMOUNT OF STUFF ON THE STACK
D2E1:              ; I.E., ANY RECURSIVE ROUTINE LIKE "FRMEVL"*
D2E1:              ; IT IS ALSO CALLED BY ROUTINES SUCH AS "GOSUB" AND "FOR"
D2E1:              ; WHICH MAKE PERMANENT ENTRIES ON THE STACK.
D2E1:              
D2E1:              ; ROUTINES WHICH MERELY USE AND FREE UP THE GUARANTEED
D2E1:              ; NUMLEV LOCATIONS NEED NOT CALL THIS.
D2E1:              
D2E1:              ; ON EXIT:

