E604:              FNWAIT:
E604: 20 c2 e5             JSR     GETNUM
E607: 86 88                STX     ANDMSK
E609: a2 00                LDX     #0
E60B: 20 b9 00             JSR     CHRGOT
E60E: f0 13   E613         BEQ     ZSTORD
E610: 20 c8 e5             JSR     COMBYT               ;GET MASK2.
E613:              STORDO:
E613: 86 89                STX     EORMSK
E615: a0 00                LDY     #0
E617:              WAITER:
E617: b1 53                LDA     (POKER),Y
E619: 45 89                EOR     EORMSK
E61B: 25 88                AND     ANDMSK
E61D: f0 17   E617         BEQ     WAITER
E61F:              ZERRTS:
E61F: 60                   RTS                          ;GOT A NONZERO.
E620:                      .subttl FLOATING POINT MATH PACKAGE CONFIGURATION.
E620:              
E620:              ;RADIX	8			;!!!! ALERT !!!!
E620:                                                   ;THROUGHOUT THE MATH PACKAGE.
E620:              
E620:              ; THE FLOATING POINT FORMAT IS AS FOLLOWS:
E620:              
E620:              ; THE SIGN IS THE FIRST BIT OF THE MANTISSA.
E620:              ; THE MANTISSA IS 24 BITS LONG.
E620:              ; THE BINARY POINT IS TO THE LEFT OF THE MSB.
E620:              ; NUMBER = MANTISSA * 2 ^ EXPONENT.
E620:              ; THE MANTISSA IS POSITIVE WITH A ONE ASSUMED TO BE WHERE THE SIGN BIT IS.
E620:              ; THE SIGN OF THE EXPONENT IS THE FIRST BIT OF THE EXPONENT.
E620:              ; THE EXPONENT IS STORED IN EXCESS 200, I.E. WITH A BIAS OF +200.
E620:              ; SO, THE EXPONENT IS A SIGNED 8-BIT NUMBER WITH 200 ADDED TO IT.
E620:              ; AN EXPONENT OF ZERO MEANS THE NUMBER IS ZERO.
E620:              ; THE OTHER BYTES MAY NOT BE ASSUMED TO BE ZERO.
E620:              ; TO KEEP THE SAME NUMBER IN THE FAC WHILE SHIFTING,
E620:              ; 	TO SHIFT RIGHT, EXP:=EXP+1
E620:              ; 	TO SHIFT LEFT,	EXP:=EXP-1
E620:              
E620:              ; IN MEMORY THE NUMBER LOOKS LIKE THIS:
E620:              ; 	[THE EXPONENT AS A SIGNED NUMBER +200]
E620:              ; 	[THE SIGN BIT IN 7, BITS 2-8 OF MANTISSA ARE IN BITS 6-0].
E620:              ; 		(REMEMBER BIT 1 OF MANTISSA IS ALWAYS A ONE.)
E620:              ; 	[BITS 9-16 OF THE MANTISSA]
E620:              ; 	[BITS 17-24] OF THE MANTISSA]
E620:              
E620:              ; ARITHMETIC ROUTINE CALLING CONVENTIONS:
E620:              
E620:              ; FOR ONE ARGUMENT FUNCTIONS:
E620:              ; 	THE ARGUMENT IS IN THE FAC.
E620:              ; 	THE RESULT IS LEFT IN THE FAC.
E620:              ; FOR TWO ARGUMENT OPERATIONS:
E620:              ; 	THE FIRST ARGUMENT IS IN ARG (ARGEXP,HO,MO,LO AND ARGSGN).
E620:              ; 	THE SECOND ARGUMENT IS IN THE FAC.
E620:              ; 	THE RESULT IS LEFT IN THE FAC.
E620:              
E620:              ; THE "T" ENTRY POINTS TO THE TWO-ARGUMENT OPERATIONS HAVE BOTH ARGUMENTS
E620:              ; SETUP IN THE RESPECTIVE REGISTERS. BEFORE CALLING ARG MAY HAVE BEEN
E620:              ; POPPED OFF THE STACK AND INTO ARG, FOR EXAMPLE.
E620:              ; THE OTHER ENTRY POINT ASSUMES [Y,A] POINTS TO THE ARGUMENT
E620:              ; SOMEWHERE IN MEMORY. IT IS UNPACKED INTO ARG BY "CONUPK".

Page 123   BASIC M6502 8K VER 1.1 BY MICRO-SOFT
          FLOATING POINT MATH PACKAGE CONFIGURATION.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
E620:              
E620:              ; ON THE STACK, THE SGN IS PUSHED ON FIRST, THE LO,MO,HO AND FINALLY EXP.
E620:              ; NOTE ALL THINGS ARE KEPT UNPACKED IN ARG, FAC AND ON THE STACK.
E620:              
E620:              ; IT IS ONLY WHEN SOMETHING IS STORED AWAY THAT IT IS PACKED TO FOUR
E620:              ; BYTES. THE UNPACKED FORMAT HAS A SGN BYTE REFLECTING THE SIGN OF THE
E620:              ; NUMBER (POSITIVE=0, NEGATIVE=-1) A HO,MO AND LO WITH THE HIGH BIT
E620:              ; OF THE HO TURNED ON. THE EXP IS THE SAME AS STORED FORMAT.
E620:              ; THIS IS DONE FOR SPEED OF OPERATION.
E620:              
E620:                      .page

