ED5C:                      .subttl EXPONENTIATION FUNCTION.
ED5C:                                                   ;FIRST SAVE THE ORIGINAL ARGUMENT AND MULTIPLY THE FAC BY
ED5C:                                                   ;LOG2(E)* THE RESULT IS USED TO DETERMINE IF OVERFLOW
ED5C:                                                   ;WILL OCCUR SINCE EXP(X)=2^(X*LOG2(E)) WHERE
ED5C:                                                   ;LOG2(E)=LOG(E) BASE 2. THEN SAVE THE INTEGER PART OF
ED5C:                                                   ;THIS TO SCALE THE ANSWER AT THE END. SINCE
ED5C:                                                   ;2^Y=2^INT(Y)*2^(Y-INT(Y)) AND 2^INT(Y) IS EASY TO COMPUTE.
ED5C:                                                   ;NOW COMPUTE 2^(X*LOG2(E)-INT(X*LOG2(E)) BY
ED5C:                                                   ;P(LN(2)*(INT(X*LOG2(E))+1)-X) WHERE P IS AN APPROXIMATION
ED5C:                                                   ;POLYNOMIAL. THE RESULT IS THEN SCALED BY THE POWER OF 2
ED5C:                                                   ;PREVIOUSLY SAVED.
ED5C:              
ED5C:              LOGEB2:
